        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Generate Person Talent Profile Markdown"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_PERSON_TALENT_PROFILE_MARKDOWN",
          "id": "1770324643255",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770324643257_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role:\nYou transform structured Person Talent Profile section JSON into deterministic, strictly formatted, LLM-friendly Markdown optimized for semantic search and embeddings.\n\nObjective:\nGiven an input JSON array of section objects, generate a clean, consistent, strictly valid Markdown document that:\n- Uses sectionContext as the primary grouping header\n- Renders sectionContent schema-agnostically (objects + arrays)\n- Deduplicates exact duplicate items within a section\n- Produces deterministic output for embedding stability\n- Uses human-readable attribute labels (Title Case) to improve semantic search alignment\n\nInput:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.textToSummarize}}\n\nINPUT FORMAT (MANDATORY ASSUMPTION):\nThe input is a JSON array. Each element is an object like:\n{\n  \"sectionContext\": \"<string>\",\n  \"sectionContent\": <object>  // may contain nested arrays/objects; may include \"contentType\"\n}\n\nSTRICT OUTPUT REQUIREMENTS (MANDATORY):\n- Output MUST be valid Markdown only.\n- Do NOT output JSON.\n- Do NOT wrap the output in code fences.\n- Do NOT include explanations or commentary.\n- Every heading MUST include proper Markdown prefixes:\n  - \"# \" for main title\n  - \"## \" for level 2\n  - \"### \" for level 3\n  - \"#### \" for level 4\n  - \"##### \" for level 5\n- Every key/value line MUST start with \"- \" (dash + space).\n- No free-form paragraphs.\n- No blank text lines except single spacing between sections.\n- If a section has no renderable fields, output:\n  - none\n\nNORMALIZATION RULES:\n- Strip HTML tags from all string values.\n- Omit attributes with null/empty values (after trimming).\n- Convert Yes/No (any case) → true/false.\n- Preserve date formats as provided.\n- Keep numbers as-is.\n- Do NOT invent fields or infer missing data.\n\nATTRIBUTE LABELING (MANDATORY):\n- Convert attribute keys into human-readable labels for output ONLY:\n  - Convert camelCase and snake_case to Title Case words separated by spaces.\n    Examples:\n      - businessUnit -> Business Unit\n      - legalEmployer -> Legal Employer\n      - reviewer_is_approved -> Reviewer Is Approved\n      - date_from -> Date From\n  - Preserve common acronyms (optional but recommended): ID, URL, GPA, HCM, ESS, SQL, AI.\n- Deduplication and ordering MUST use the ORIGINAL keys, not the transformed labels.\n- Only the rendered output uses the transformed labels.\n\nDETERMINISTIC ORDERING (MANDATORY):\n1) Document header\n2) Sections sorted alphabetically by sectionContext (case-insensitive)\n3) Within each section:\n   a) Render sectionContent keys alphabetically by ORIGINAL key (case-insensitive)\n   b) If sectionContent contains arrays (e.g., \"Competencies\": [ ... ]), treat each array name as a subgroup (alphabetical)\n   c) Within each subgroup array: items sorted alphabetically by primary identifier\n   d) Within each item: attributes sorted alphabetically by ORIGINAL attribute key\n\nPRIMARY IDENTIFIER PRIORITY (for sorting + item heading):\n1) name\n2) title\n3) certificate_number\n4) \"Item <index>\"\n\nDEDUPLICATION:\n- Deduplicate exact duplicate items within the same sectionContext + subgroup.\n- Duplicates = same normalized primary identifier AND identical rendered attributes after normalization.\n- Keep only one instance of identical items.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\nREQUIRED MARKDOWN STRUCTURE (FOLLOW EXACTLY)\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\n# Person Talent Profile\n\n## Talent Profile Sections\n\nFor each section element in the input array:\n\n### Section: <sectionContext>\n\nIf sectionContent includes a \"contentType\" value:\n- Content Type: <value>\n\nThen render sectionContent as follows:\n\nA) If sectionContent is a simple object with only scalar values (no arrays/objects):\n- <Label(Key)>: <value>\n- <Label(Key)>: <value>\n\nB) If sectionContent contains one or more arrays (e.g., \"Competencies\": [ ... ]):\nFor each array key (subgroup) in sectionContent (excluding \"contentType\"):\n\n#### <Label(array_key)>\nFor each item in the array:\n\n##### <Primary Identifier>\n- <Label(attribute_key)>: <value>\n- <Label(attribute_key)>: <value>\n\nC) If sectionContent contains nested objects (non-array) besides scalars:\nRender nested objects deterministically, flattening one level using \"<parent>.<child>\" labels:\n- <Label(parent)>.<Label(child)>: <value>\n\nIf nothing remains after normalization:\n- none\n\nFINAL VALIDATION BEFORE OUTPUT:\n- Confirm output starts with \"# Person Talent Profile\".\n- Confirm all headings use \"#\" syntax.\n- Confirm all key/value lines begin with \"- \".\n- Confirm no JSON braces \"{\", \"}\", \"[\" , \"]\" appear.\n- Confirm no explanatory prose appears.\n\nNow generate the Markdown strictly following the above structure from the provided JSON input."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
      "rootNode": "start",
